<<~ ahu slot=`#/witness-rule`>>

!! (e) Witness rule

Extend `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs:143-151` with a tracked-file test census for exact retired-name assertions in house tests. Match negative checks such as `not.toContain("readExchanges")`, literal retired command arrays, and old-name URL/env fixtures; require each exception to name a present hostile-input grammar or external protocol, using the existing stale-exception accounting at `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs:114-125` (`packages/lares-cli/tests/turn-key-one-leg.test.ts:26-39`; `packages/lares-cli/tests/unknown-command-refuses.test.ts:23-55`; `packages/lararium-node/tests/flow-closed-door.test.ts:94-103`; `packages/lararium-node/tests/lares-config.test.ts:80-89`). Add a narrow persistence check for `deleteObjectStore` and a writer/reader pairing check for a second house spelling; the concrete seeds stand at `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-vessel-identity.ts:99-119` and `packages/lararium-mesh/src/agile-digest.ts:100-129`. A generic malformed-input test stays allowed because `packages/lararium-memetic-frame/tests/verdict.test.ts:74-96` exercises bytes a reader may meet from outside.

